  "issues": [
    "CRITICAL FACTUAL ERROR — Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct InfoVQA zero-shot baseline: The proposal repeatedly states 'the expected Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct zero-shot range (80–84%) based on scaling trends from Qwen2.5-VL-7B' and explicitly asserts this is 'unconfirmed in any public source.' This is wrong. DocCogito (arXiv:2603.07494, March 2026) — which the proposal cites as a key reference — explicitly reports Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct zero-shot InfoVQA = 75.7 ANLS. DocCogito-8B achieves 78.6 ANLS, a +2.9 improvement over zero-shot. The proposal's central argument that 'DocCogito's 78.6% is below the expected 80-84% zero-shot baseline — confirming implicit layout representation learning is insufficient' is factually inverted: DocCogito OUTPERFORMS the zero-shot baseline by ~3 points. This error appears in the core_problem, opportunity, landscape, and description fields. EMNLP reviewers familiar with DocCogito will immediately identify this.",
    "CONSEQUENTIAL NARRATIVE ERROR — DocCogito motivation framing: Because the zero-shot baseline is 75.7% (not 80-84%), the argument that 'DocCogito confirms implicit layout tokens are insufficient for hard multi-hop layout questions' is unsupported. DocCogito shows implicit layout tokens DO help (+2.9 points). The correct framing is: 'DocCogito-8B improves modestly over zero-shot (+2.9 ANLS) but remains 5.6 points below the best open-source single-model result; LHEC hypothesizes that explicit typed graph traversal training yields larger gains on hard multi-hop questions by encoding structured spatial semantics (Caption-of, Adjacent) directly supervising the reasoning chain.' This is still a valid and differentiating argument — it just needs to be stated correctly.",
    "MINOR CITATION ACCURACY — Qwen2.5-VL-72B 84.2% source: The proposal states 'best open-source single-model zero-shot result is Qwen2.5-VL-72B-Instruct at 84.2% ANLS (as reported in the SV paper).' Independent verification of the SV paper (ICLR 2026, arXiv:2510.20812) shows the draft models are Qwen2.5-VL-7B-Instruct (79.8%), not 72B. The 84.2% figure may be correct but the attribution 'as reported in the SV paper' appears inaccurate — it likely comes from DocCogito's comparison table or a separate leaderboard source. Correct the citation source.",
    "MINOR NUMERICAL DISCREPANCY — WikiMixQA InternVL2.5-78B oracle score: The proposal states 27.37% for InternVL2.5-78B in the oracle setting. The WikiMixQA paper HTML (verified) reports 27.67%. This is a minor discrepancy that should be corrected for submission accuracy."
  ],
  "feedback": "Round 9 has successfully resolved all issues from Rounds 1-8: timeline and compute meet hard constraints, DocCogito is cited with four-axis differentiation, WikiMixQA oracle protocol is specified, LayoutLLM/DocLayLLM/PDF-VQA/MGA-VQA are correctly positioned, Day 0/1 prerequisites are explicit with threshold-gated framing, and InfographicVQA hard subset is the primary contribution claim. One new factual error — introduced when DocCogito was added — blocks a pass.\n\n**Fix 1 (Critical — Qwen3-VL-8B InfoVQA baseline):** DocCogito's paper (which you cite as a key reference) reports Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct zero-shot InfoVQA = 75.7 ANLS. Replace every occurrence of 'likely in the 80-84 range based on scaling trends' and 'unconfirmed in any public source' with: 'Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct zero-shot InfoVQA = 75.7 ANLS (per DocCogito Table X; Day 1 zero-shot eval will confirm).' Day 1 evaluation remains a good prerequisite but the estimate is now 75.7 not 80-84.\n\n**Fix 2 (Critical — DocCogito motivation reframe):** Since DocCogito-8B (78.6%) outperforms its own Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct zero-shot baseline (75.7%) by +2.9 points, the argument 'DocCogito's training fails to reach zero-shot level, confirming implicit layout tokens are insufficient' is wrong. Replace with: 'DocCogito-8B improves over the Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct zero-shot baseline by +2.9 ANLS (75.7 → 78.6), but the gap between its implicit layout token approach and the best open-source single-model result (84.2% for Qwen2.5-VL-72B, a 9× larger model) remains 5.6 points. LHEC hypothesizes that explicit typed spatial graph traversal — directly encoding Caption-of, Adjacent, and directional edges into supervised reasoning chains — achieves larger gains on hard multi-hop layout questions than DocCogito's implicit global layout priors, with a substantially simpler training pipeline.' This framing is empirically accurate and still strongly motivates LHEC.\n\n**Fix 3 (Minor — source citation):** Verify and correct the source for 'Qwen2.5-VL-72B at 84.2% ANLS.' If this figure comes from DocCogito's Table 1 comparison, cite DocCogito rather than the SV paper. The SV paper reports Qwen2.5-VL-7B (79.8%) as a draft model, not 72B.\n\n**Fix 4 (Minor — WikiMixQA score):** Correct InternVL2.5-78B oracle score to 27.67% (from paper HTML) vs. the 27.37% currently cited.",
  "reason": "All Round 1-8 issues resolved, but the proposal contains a critical factual error introduced when DocCogito was added: Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct InfoVQA zero-shot is 75.7% (confirmed from DocCogito's own tables), not the claimed 80-84%, meaning DocCogito actually improves over zero-shot rather than failing below it — a factual inversion that EMNLP reviewers will catch."
}
